// Jest Snapshot v1, https://jestjs.io/docs/snapshot-testing

exports[`CLI help interface for 'config-manager pull oauth-clients' should be expected english 1`] = `
"Usage: frodo config-manager pull oauth-clients [options] [host] [realm] [username] [password]

[Experimental] Export the OAuth2 clients of all realms or of one realm to
realms/<realm>/realm-config/agents/OAuth2Client/<id>.json, one file for each.
The files are the ones that the deprecated "pull oauth2-agents" writes for the
OAuth2 clients, at the same paths. The other agent types are pulled by "pull
agents".

Arguments:
  host                  AM base URL, e.g.: https://cdk.iam.example.com/am. To
                        use a connection profile, just specify a unique
                        substring or alias.
  realm                 Realm. Specify realm as '/' for the root realm or
                        'realm' or '/parent/child' otherwise. (default: "alpha"
                        for Identity Cloud tenants, "/" otherwise.)
  username              Username to login with. Must be an admin user with
                        appropriate rights to manage authentication
                        journeys/trees. If given without a password, and it
                        matches the username already stored in the connection
                        profile for the target host, frodo uses that profile's
                        stored password instead of requiring it on the command
                        line.
  password              Password.

Options:
  --allow-failures      Report operations that fail, but still exit with code 0.
                        Without this option the command runs every operation,
                        prints a summary of what failed and exits with code 1.
  --config-file <file>  A JSON file that lists the OAuth2 clients to pull for
                        each realm, with overrides. ex: "oauth2-agents.json".
                        Without it, every OAuth2 client of every realm is
                        pulled. The realm argument narrows a pull without a
                        file; with a file the realms of the file are pulled and
                        the realm argument is not used. Cannot be used with -i.
  -i, --client-id <id>  OAuth2 client id. If specified, pulls only that client.
                        Needs a single realm (the realm argument). Cannot be
                        used with --config-file.
  -h, --help            Help
  -hh, --help-more      Help with all options.
  -hhh, --help-all      Help with all options, environment variables, and usage
                        examples.
"
`;
